   "Statement": "<b>Occupation</b><br>District Court Judge 2022-Present, Tacoma Municipal Court Judge 2019-2022, Judge Pro Tempore, Attorney.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\"><br><b>Education</b><br>Seattle University School of Law; Morehouse College; Tacoma Public Schools.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br><b>Statement</b><br>Judge Dwayne Christopher is a committed and dedicated jurist who has served our community throughout his career. A proud son of educators, Dwayne Christopher is the embodiment of what matters most in our judges. Dedication to the law. Commitment to community. And the judicial temperament to ensure fairness in the Courtroom.&nbsp;</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">Judge Christopher was first elected to the Tacoma Municipal Court Bench in 2018 and four years later he was unanimously appointed to the District Court Bench.&nbsp; In the past eight years as a Judge, Dwayne Christopher has earned an outstanding reputation for his willingness to ensure that each party in his Courtroom can present their case to a person who listens. Dwayne possesses the calm demeanor, respect and objectivity needed to resolve the complex cases brought before the District Court Bench. Judge Christopher currently presides over Veterans Treatment Court.</p><p></p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">&nbsp;Please vote to reelect Judge Dwayne Christopher. Thank you.</p><p> </p><p style=\"margin: 0px; padding: 0px;\">",
